{
  "@context": "http://schema.org/",
  "@type": "JobPosting",
  "title": "Product Operations Manager (remote Europe)",
  "description": "&lt;p&gt;Spacelift is the infrastructure orchestration platform built for the modern software era, managing the full lifecycle for both traditional IaC and AI-accelerated infrastructure. It integrates with Terraform, OpenTofu, CloudFormation, Pulumi, and Ansible in a single governed workflow so you deliver secure, compliant infrastructure at scale. Developer self-service, Golden Paths with guardrails, an OPA policy engine, and drift detection accelerate developer velocity while maintaining control. Spacelift Intelligence adds AI-powered provisioning and diagnostics across traditional and AI-driven workflows.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Spacelift was founded in 2020 by long-time DevOps practitioner Marcin Wyszynski and successful entrepreneur Pawel Hytry and has raised $82.3M in funding over four rounds from top venture capital firms including Insight Partners, Blossom Capital, Hoxton Ventures, Inovo Venture partners and Five Elms Capital.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h6&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The role:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h6&gt;&lt;p&gt;Product &amp;amp; Design at Spacelift is scaling its surface area: more product teams, more cross-functional partners and a way of working we are actively reshaping.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;We need someone who keeps that machine running. Someone who owns the tooling, the rituals, the data, and the customer feedback loop so that PMs, designers, and Epic Owners spend their time on product decisions, not chasing reports, hunting templates, or stitching together feedback from five places.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h6&gt;About you:&lt;/h6&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ve been doing product analytics, product ops, or a hybrid PM-adjacent role and want to broaden into operations.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;You&#39;re fluent in SQL and comfortable working with product analytics tools (Mixpanel, Metabase, Amplitude, or similar).&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;You&#39;re organised in a way that makes other people more effective. You build systems, not just lists.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;You can hold the line on process without becoming process for its own sake. &quot;Do not fall in love with process.&quot;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;You&#39;re comfortable working across Engineering, Design, Sales, Marketing, CS, Support, and Solutions Engineering.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;You&#39;re intellectually humble. You ask good questions, you change your mind when the data says so.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;Fluent English&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;h6&gt;Nice to have:&lt;/h6&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;Experience with infrastructure, DevOps, or developer-tools products.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;Familiarity with Working Backwards / PR-FAQ as a framework.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;Experience administering ClickUp or Notion.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;Background working alongside design and research (Figma, discovery interviews).&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;h6&gt;What you will do:&lt;/h6&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;Own and administer the Product &amp;amp; Design tool stack (Notion, Mixpanel, Metabase, Hex, Featurebase, Figma) and keep it working as a coherent system&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;Run product process rituals: weekly syncs, epic demos, kickoffs, retros, pre-mortems, and quarterly planning&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;Build and maintain KPI, adoption, and usability dashboards; write SQL and build visualizations directly; partner with PMs on discovery analytics&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;Design and operate the customer feedback pipeline — consolidating signals from six channels (Featurebase, Sales, CS, Support, CAB, discovery interviews) into a weekly digest routed to the right PM at the right time&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;Track which customer requests turned into shipped features, in-progress work, or deliberate declines, and close the loop back to Sales and CS&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;Maintain PR/FAQ and 5 Questions templates in Notion; track which initiatives have artifacts, which are missing them, and surface gaps to the SVP of Product &amp;amp; Design&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;Coordinate cross-functional release logistics with Marketing, Sales, CS, Support, and Solutions Engineering&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;Advocate for data hygiene: consistent event taxonomy, instrumentation standards, clean property naming&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Hiring Process:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;Intro interview with &lt;a target=&quot;_blank&quot; href=&quot;https://www.linkedin.com/in/olga-gradowska-pernak-123550175/&quot;&gt;Olga Gradowska-Pernak&lt;/a&gt;, Technical Recruiter&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;Hiring Manager interview with &lt;a target=&quot;_blank&quot; href=&quot;https://www.linkedin.com/in/jkowall/&quot;&gt;Jonah Kowall&lt;/a&gt;, SVP of Product &amp;amp; Design&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;Take-home exercise&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;Home Assignment Debriefing Session with the Product Team&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why Spacelift?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Innovative Culture&lt;/strong&gt;: Join a team shaping cloud infrastructure management’s future.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Growth Opportunities&lt;/strong&gt;: Be a key player in driving Spacelift’s business and AWS partnership to new heights.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Work-Life Balance&lt;/strong&gt;: Flexible work environment, with remote-first options and competitive compensation packages.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Collaborative Team&lt;/strong&gt;: Work with passionate, talented people committed to driving success for our customers and partners.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Our values&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;notion-enable-hover&quot; style=&quot;font-weight:600;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;We build for CUSTOMERS&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;notion-enable-hover&quot; style=&quot;font-weight:600;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;We RESPECT each other&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;notion-enable-hover&quot; style=&quot;font-weight:600;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;We take OWNERSHIP seriously&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;notion-enable-hover&quot; style=&quot;font-weight:600;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;We succeed through COLLABORATION&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;notion-enable-hover&quot; style=&quot;font-weight:600;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;We embrace SPARK &amp;amp; WONDER&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;p&gt;More here: &lt;a target=&quot;_blank&quot; href=&quot;https://spacelift.io/careers&quot;&gt;https://spacelift.io/careers&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Join Us! At Spacelift, you won’t just be working on a technical product - you’ll be part of a team shaping the future of DevOps. Apply to contribute to a platform loved by its users and take your career to the next level!&lt;/p&gt;",
